        <summary>thinkorswim Desktop is the advanced trading platform from Charles Schwab for stocks, options, futures, and forex with charting, scanning, and analytical tools.</summary>
        <description>### Note

This Chocolatey package downloads the official thinkorswim Desktop installer from Charles Schwab's CDN and runs it in unattended/silent mode. The application itself is owned and copyrighted by Charles Schwab &amp; Co., Inc.; this package is community-maintained for automated deployment.

### thinkorswim Desktop

[thinkorswim](https://www.schwab.com/trading/thinkorswim/desktop) is the desktop trading platform from Charles Schwab (formerly TD Ameritrade) for traders who need advanced charting, customizable studies, real-time scanning, options analysis, and direct market access across equities, options, futures, and forex.

A funded Schwab brokerage account is required to log in and trade. A paperMoney (virtual trading) account is available for practice without a funded account.

### Installer behaviour

The vendor's installer is built with [install4j](https://www.ej-technologies.com/products/install4j/overview.html) and supports unattended installation via standard install4j flags. This package runs:

```
thinkorswim_x64_installer.exe -q -overwrite
```

- `-q` &#8212; quiet mode, no UI shown
- `-overwrite` &#8212; allow overwriting an existing install of the same version

The installer's bundled JRE is extracted alongside the application; no separate Java install is required.

### Package parameters

Override install4j flags by passing additional arguments via `--params`:

```
choco install thinkorswim --params "/install-dir=C:\Apps\thinkorswim"
```

| Parameter | Effect |
|---|---|
| `/install-dir=&lt;path&gt;` | Override the installer's default install location (passed through as install4j's `-dir &lt;path&gt;`) |

### Uninstall

The package's `chocolateyUninstall.ps1` discovers the uninstaller via the registry `UninstallString` and runs it with install4j's `-q` flag.

### Verification

`tools\VERIFICATION.txt` records the upstream URL, the pinned SHA256 checksum of the installer at package time, and the steps to reproduce the checksum locally.</description>
